   "id": "camps",
   "title": "Two camps north of Adrianople",
   "time": "6-8 August 378",
   "narrative": "Valens has gathered his field army at Adrianople and fortified a camp with ditch and rampart, leaving the treasury and officials inside. Scouts report a Gothic force of about ten thousand twenty-five kilometres to the north. Richomeres arrives with a letter from Gratian asking him to wait for the western reinforcements, and the officers agree, but Valens wants a victory of his own. On 8 August Fritigern offers peace in exchange for land, and Valens refuses.",
