   "time": "Morning to noon, 9 August",
   "narrative": "Valens leaves Adrianople at dawn and marches about eight Roman miles over rough ground, arriving around noon. His men are tired and thirsty after the August heat. The Gothic camp sits on rising ground, with the wagon circle protecting families and goods. Fritigern's aim is to stall, because Alatheus, Saphrax and the Gothic horse are away foraging.",
