   "id": "stall",
   "title": "Smoke and negotiation",
   "time": "Early afternoon",
   "narrative": "The Goths set fire to the fields so that smoke and heat harass the approaching Romans. Envoys cross between the lines to arrange an exchange of hostages. Each hour of talk costs the Romans water and patience, while it buys Fritigern time for his cavalry. Valens forms his army into line facing the hill, with infantry in the centre and horse on the flanks. The exact order is not given in the sources.",
