  {
   "id": "scholae",
   "title": "The scholae charge without orders",
   "time": "Mid-afternoon",
   "narrative": "Before talks conclude, some Roman units open the fight on their own. The imperial scholae, shield bearers and archers under the Iberian prince Bacurius, rush ahead, hoping for an easy win and revenge for two years of raiding. With no support behind them, they are pushed back by the Gothic defenders. The assault shows the discipline breaking and drags the whole line into battle before it is ready.",
